{
  "topic": "tunguska",
  "ttsScript": "June 30th, 1908. The largest explosion in recorded history hit Siberia. No crater. No meteorite. No explanation for 19 years. Locals thought a god was punishing them. Scientists guessed a volcano. Then a comet. Every theory fell apart. 80 million trees flattened in a radial pattern. 2,150 square kilometers destroyed. The shockwave registered in London. Night skies glowed for weeks. But there was no crater. No fragments. It was an airburst. A rock 50 meters wide exploded kilometers above the surface. Vaporized before impact. The ground was hit by pure energy. A rock the size of a building destroyed an area the size of a city. And left absolutely nothing behind.",
